9098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-02-16T06:56:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T15:46:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- 4.4-beta3\n\n### System information\n\nNot relevant\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using Godot 4.4 [typed dictionaries](#78656), it is possible to assign the incorrect key type to a dictionary and receive an unhelpful error message as to the type of the key begin assigned:\n\n> Invalid assignment of property or key '(-1, 0)' with value of type 'Resource (HexTile)' on a base object of type 'Dictionary[Vector2i, HexTile]'.\n\nHere, specifically, the error message should state what the type of the key being attempted to be assigned is. In this case it's clear that it's a `Vector2i`, but that can only be inferred from the format of the printout and may not be accurate.\n\nFor context, I'm creating a [serialization library for Godot 4.4](https://github.com/abstractionfactory/estragon)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\nvar dict : Dictionary[Vector2i,String] = {}\n# This is intentional to make it reproducible on a small scale:\nvar key : Variant = Vector3i(1,2,3)\nvar value : String = \"Hello world!\"\ndict[key] = value\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18813864/project.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102909/reactions","total_count":0,